{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/leecdiang/HeteroSpec/pulls/162","id":5120077555,"node_id":"PR_kwDOUQYb288AAAABMS4u8w","html_url":"https://github.com/leecdiang/HeteroSpec/pull/162","diff_url":"https://github.com/leecdiang/HeteroSpec/pull/162.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/leecdiang/HeteroSpec/pull/162.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/leecdiang/HeteroSpec/issues/162","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/leecdiang/HeteroSpec/pulls/162/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/leecdiang/HeteroSpec/pulls/162/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/leecdiang/HeteroSpec/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/leecdiang/HeteroSpec/issues/162/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/leecdiang/HeteroSpec/statuses/e11d2b75d82422409ba2b701aa38c59f36acc50b","number":162,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Llama RTX repair: unseen qualification passes; layout gain below noise screen","user":{"login":"leecdiang","id":162876606,"node_id":"U_kgDOCbVMvg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/162876606?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/leecdiang","html_url":"https://github.com/leecdiang","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leecdiang/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leecdiang/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leecdiang/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leecdiang/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leecdiang/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leecdiang/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leecdiang/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leecdiang/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leecdiang/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"This independent result PR executes PR160 and preserves the original R, historical failures and cumulative budget. No earlier PR is merged and no manuscript is edited.\n\nThe Llama failure is traced to physical KV reduction extent, not assumed to be Qwen RoPE. All 54 PR151 diagnostics and 5,916 complete vectors were authenticated. Default native compilation and capacity admission reproduced the old failure. Same-state consumers, both orders, own-path/trace controls, 22 native operator replays and crossed-extent interventions support a guarded prefix-extent repair. Ablation restores both original C-arm failures. Failed observers/candidates and all source versions remain retained.\n\nCompleted native validation and independent reconstruction:\n- New Qwen8B/14B regressions: 144/192 requests, plus 24/32 successful immutable original-R requests with complete-vector preservation.\n- Fixed 24 unseen inputs: 48 original-R references and 240 candidate qualification requests pass. Independent audit checks 23,080 complete vectors, 168 candidate final states, endpoints, transactions, observer pairs, geometry and selection provenance.\n- Six complete Williams sessions: 864 measured requests plus 864 warmups. Independent reconstruction verifies every record, registered order and balance, immediate warmups and all costs.\n\nC_QB / arithmetic-dual-C_PQ geometric mean service ratio is **0.975530833**: a **2.4469%** reduction. Every session favors QB, but the maximum symmetric input-aggregate A/A imbalance is **2.9832%**. Therefore the prospective practical layout-gain screen **does not pass**. No extra timing or block selection is used to change that result. No population confidence interval is claimed.\n\nThe unchanged cumulative new-study ledger reserves 2,862 work credits (846 development), with 2,573 audited complete model requests, 22 standalone operator replays and 130 extra shadow decodes. Six failed native units remain charged, alongside failed preparation/schema operations and built/unlaunched configurations. Historical ledgers remain separate.\n\nScientific source/data snapshot: `70086c63af202cd844a3062eff3929218152f73c`. See `benchmarks/rtx_llama_repair_v1/host_execution/RESULTS.md`, `PAPER_ADDENDUM.md`, `FINAL_EXECUTION_SUMMARY.json`, `records/` and `RESTORE.md`.\n\n**Delivery in progress:** full raw/source archive, upload and fresh every-member remote readback. The evidence release remains a draft until all delivery gates pass; final asset links and receipts will be added here.","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-11-02T12:10:43Z","updated_at":"2026-11-02T18:41:45Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"50f26bef5fbfe92224ea07493890045c05dcd627","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"leecdiang:codex/pr160-llama-repair","ref":"codex/pr160-llama-repair","repo":{"id":1359354843,"node_id":"R_kgDOUQYb2w","name":"HeteroSpec","full_name":"leecdiang/HeteroSpec","owner":{"login":"leecdiang","id":162876606,"node_id":"U_kgDOCbVMvg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/162876606?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/leecdiang","html_url":"https://github.com/leecdiang","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leecdiang/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leecdiang/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leecdiang/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leecdiang/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leecdiang/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leecdiang/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leecdiang/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leecdiang/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leecdiang/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"private":true,"fork":false,"archived":false,"disabled":false,"description":"Chara